# R3 Part 5（30 題）與 Part 6（4 篇 16 格）。ans 一律 0，執行時洗牌。
# Part 5 類別比照 R2：詞性 8、介係詞 5、詞彙 7、連接詞 3、關係詞 2、動詞時態 2、分詞 1、代名詞 1、比較級 1
P5 = [
 ("The renovation of the main lobby was completed ______ ahead of schedule.", ["slightly", "slight", "slighted", "slightness"], "詞性",
  "修飾副詞片語 ahead of schedule，要用副詞 slightly（稍微）：比預定稍早完成。slight 是形容詞；slighted 是過去分詞（被輕視的）；slightness 是名詞。"),
 ("Ms. Han's ______ to the project was praised by the entire team.", ["contribution", "contribute", "contributed", "contributing"], "詞性",
  "所有格 Ms. Han's 後面接名詞，而且是句子的主詞：contribution（貢獻）。contribute 是動詞原形；contributed、contributing 不能接在所有格後面當主詞。"),
 ("All visitors must wear ______ identification badges while on the factory floor.", ["visible", "visibly", "visibility", "visualize"], "詞性",
  "名詞片語 identification badges 前面要形容詞：visible（看得見的、明顯的）。visibly 是副詞；visibility 是名詞；visualize 是動詞。"),
 ("The board will vote on the proposal after a ______ review of the budget.", ["thorough", "thoroughly", "thoroughness", "more thoroughly"], "詞性",
  "冠詞 a 和名詞 review 之間要形容詞：thorough（徹底的）。thoroughly、more thoroughly 是副詞；thoroughness 是名詞。"),
 ("Customer complaints have decreased ______ since the company introduced its online chat service.", ["significantly", "significant", "significance", "signify"], "詞性",
  "修飾動詞 have decreased，要用副詞 significantly（大幅地）。significant 是形容詞；significance 是名詞；signify 是動詞。"),
 ("The museum's new wing is expected to attract a ______ number of tourists.", ["considerable", "considerably", "consideration", "considerate"], "詞性",
  "a ___ number of 中間要形容詞，表示「相當多的」：considerable。considerate 也是形容詞，但意思是「體貼的」，不能修飾 number；considerably 是副詞；consideration 是名詞。"),
 ("Please read the safety instructions ______ before operating the machine.", ["carefully", "careful", "care", "cared"], "詞性",
  "修飾動詞 read，要用副詞 carefully（仔細地）。careful 是形容詞；care 是名詞或動詞；cared 是過去式。"),
 ("The company's ______ in the Asian market has exceeded expectations.", ["expansion", "expand", "expanded", "expansive"], "詞性",
  "所有格 The company's 後面接名詞當主詞：expansion（擴張）。expand 是動詞；expanded 是過去式或過去分詞；expansive 是形容詞。"),
 ("The conference room is unavailable ______ noon and 2 P.M. on Thursday.", ["between", "from", "during", "throughout"], "介係詞",
  "between A and B（在 A 和 B 之間）。from 要搭配 to；during、throughout 後面接一段期間的名詞，不接 A and B。"),
 ("Ms. Patel will be responsible ______ training the new sales staff.", ["for", "to", "with", "of"], "介係詞",
  "be responsible for（負責某事）是固定搭配。be responsible to 是「對某人負責」，後面接人，不接 training。"),
 ("The shipment was delayed ______ a shortage of trucks.", ["because of", "although", "in spite of", "so that"], "介係詞",
  "後面是名詞片語 a shortage of trucks，又表示原因，用介係詞片語 because of。although、so that 是連接詞，後面要接子句；in spite of 意思相反（儘管）。"),
 ("The library is located ______ the street from the city hall.", ["across", "through", "along", "over"], "介係詞",
  "across the street from（在…的對街）是固定說法。through、along、over 都不能和 the street from 搭配出這個意思。"),
 ("Registration for the workshop must be completed ______ October 15.", ["by", "until", "within", "since"], "介係詞",
  "截止期限用 by（在…之前完成）。until 表示動作持續到某時，和「完成」不搭；within 後面接一段時間（within two weeks）；since 要搭配完成式。"),
 ("The marketing team will ______ the results of the survey at next week's meeting.", ["present", "attend", "appear", "occur"], "詞彙",
  "在會議上「報告、提出」調查結果：present。attend 是「參加」，受詞要是會議；appear、occur 是不及物動詞，不能接受詞。"),
 ("Due to high demand, the new model is currently out of ______.", ["stock", "order", "service", "place"], "詞彙",
  "需求很高，所以「缺貨」：out of stock。out of order 是「故障」；out of service 是「停止運作」；out of place 是「格格不入」，都不符合需求高的語意。"),
 ("The hotel offers a complimentary shuttle service to guests who ______ a room for three nights or more.", ["reserve", "conserve", "preserve", "deserve"], "詞彙",
  "預訂房間：reserve。conserve（節約）、preserve（保存）、deserve（應得）字形相近，但意思不合。"),
 ("Mr. Ito was promoted to regional manager in ______ of his outstanding sales record.", ["recognition", "admission", "reputation", "attention"], "詞彙",
  "in recognition of（表彰、肯定…）是固定片語：因為業績優異而升職。in admission of、in reputation of、in attention of 都不是正確的片語。"),
 ("Before signing the contract, please make sure that all the ______ are correct.", ["details", "detours", "debates", "devices"], "詞彙",
  "簽約前確認所有「細節」正確：details。detours（繞道）、debates（辯論）、devices（裝置）都不能形容合約內容是否正確。"),
 ("The factory has been running at full ______ since it received the large order.", ["capacity", "possibility", "quality", "quantity"], "詞彙",
  "at full capacity（滿載、全力生產）是固定搭配。full possibility、full quality、full quantity 都不是這個意思的說法。"),
 ("Employees are ______ to submit their travel expenses within thirty days.", ["required", "considered", "proposed", "insisted"], "詞彙",
  "be required to（被要求、必須）。be considered to 是「被認為」；proposed 不用 be proposed to do 表示規定；insist 要接 on，沒有 be insisted to 的用法。"),
 ("______ the weather was poor, the outdoor concert went ahead as planned.", ["Although", "Because", "Unless", "Provided that"], "連接詞",
  "天氣不好，音樂會卻照常舉行，前後是讓步關係：Although（雖然）。Because 表示原因，語意相反；Unless（除非）和 Provided that（只要）都不合。"),
 ("The report will be distributed to all staff ______ it has been approved by the director.", ["once", "while", "unless", "whereas"], "連接詞",
  "「一旦」主管核准就發給所有人：once。while 表示同時或對比；unless（除非）會變成「除非已核准才不發」，語意不合；whereas 表示對比。"),
 ("Customers can pay ______ by credit card or by bank transfer.", ["either", "both", "neither", "whether"], "連接詞",
  "either A or B（A 或 B 擇一）。both 要搭配 and；neither 要搭配 nor；whether A or B 用在子句（不管是…還是…），不能直接接在 pay 後面表示付款方式。"),
 ("The candidate ______ we interviewed yesterday has accepted our offer.", ["whom", "whose", "what", "which"], "關係詞",
  "先行詞是人（The candidate），在關係子句中當 interviewed 的受詞：whom。whose 後面要接名詞；what 不能有先行詞；which 不能指人。"),
 ("The supplier, ______ prices are the lowest in the region, has been our partner for ten years.", ["whose", "who", "which", "that"], "關係詞",
  "空格後面直接接名詞 prices（供應商的價格），表示所有關係：whose。who、which 後面要接動詞或缺主詞／受詞的子句；that 不能用在逗號後的非限定子句。"),
 ("By the time the new manager arrives next month, the renovation ______.", ["will have been completed", "has been completed", "was completed", "is completing"], "動詞時態",
  "By the time + 未來的時間點（下個月經理到任時），主要子句用未來完成式；整修是被完成，所以是被動：will have been completed。"),
 ("Mr. Lopez ______ for the company for fifteen years before he retired last spring.", ["had worked", "has worked", "has been working", "will work"], "動詞時態",
  "退休（去年春天）是過去的事，在那之前已經工作了十五年：過去完成式 had worked。has worked、has been working 是現在完成式，不能搭配已經退休的過去時間點。"),
 ("The documents ______ to the application must be signed by a supervisor.", ["attached", "attaching", "attach", "attachment"], "分詞",
  "文件是「被附上」的，用過去分詞 attached 修飾 documents（＝documents that are attached）。attaching 是主動；attach 是動詞原形；attachment 是名詞。"),
 ("Ms. Chen prefers to review the contracts ______ rather than rely on her assistant.", ["herself", "her", "hers", "themselves"], "代名詞",
  "強調「親自」審閱，用反身代名詞 herself。her、hers 放在句尾不能表示「自己親自」；themselves 是複數，和 Ms. Chen 不一致。"),
 ("This year's sales figures are ______ than those of any previous year.", ["higher", "highest", "high", "more high"], "比較級",
  "後面有 than，要用比較級；high 是單音節形容詞，比較級是 higher。highest 是最高級；more high 不是正確形式。"),
]

P6 = [
 ("電子郵件：辦公室搬遷",
  "To: All Staff\nFrom: Facilities Department\nSubject: Office move\n\nAs you know, our team will move to the new building on Grant Street next month. To make the transition as smooth as possible, we ask that you ___[1]___ your personal belongings by Friday, March 7. Boxes and labels will be ___[2]___ at the front desk starting Monday. ___[3]___\n\nThe movers will transport all furniture and computer equipment over the weekend. ___[4]___, please contact Ana Ruiz at extension 214.",
  [(["pack", "packed", "packing", "to pack"], "ask that + 主詞 + 原形動詞（假設語氣）：we ask that you pack。packed、packing、to pack 都不能放在 that 子句的主詞 you 後面當動詞。"),
   (["available", "availability", "avail", "availably"], "be 動詞後面接形容詞：will be available（可以取得）。availability 是名詞；avail 是動詞；availably 不是常用字。"),
   (["Please write your name and new desk number on each box.", "The new building has a large cafeteria on the top floor.", "Last year's move was postponed because of bad weather.", "Staff parking will cost ten dollars per day."],
    "句子插入題：前一句說櫃台會發箱子和標籤，接著說明標籤要寫什麼（姓名和新座位號碼）最連貫。餐廳、去年延期、停車費都和打包的指示無關。"),
   (["If you have any questions", "Even so", "As a result", "In addition"], "後面是 please contact…（請聯絡…），前面需要一個條件：If you have any questions（如果有任何問題）。Even so（即便如此）、As a result（結果）、In addition（此外）都不能引出「請聯絡某人」。")]),
 ("廣告：烹飪學校週末課程",
  "Riverside Cooking School is pleased to announce a new series of weekend classes for beginners. Each class is ___[1]___ by a professional chef and lasts three hours. Participants will learn basic knife skills, simple sauces, and ___[2]___ to plan balanced meals.\n\nAll ingredients and equipment are provided. ___[3]___ Class sizes are limited to twelve students, so early registration is ___[4]___ recommended.",
  [(["taught", "teaching", "teach", "teacher"], "課程是「被教授」的，is + 過去分詞的被動：is taught by a professional chef。teaching 會變成課程在教別人；teach 和 teacher 不能接在 is 後面。"),
   (["how", "what", "which", "why"], "learn how to plan（學習如何規劃）。what to plan 是「規劃什麼」，和後面的 balanced meals 不搭；which、why 也不合。"),
   (["Students simply need to bring an apron.", "Our restaurant is open every evening except Monday.", "The school was founded by two brothers in 1998.", "Advanced classes require a written test."],
    "句子插入題：前一句說食材和器材都由學校提供，接著說「學生只要帶圍裙」最連貫。文中沒有提到餐廳；學校歷史和進階班考試都和初學者課程的準備無關。"),
   (["strongly", "strong", "strength", "strengthen"], "修飾形容詞 recommended，要用副詞：strongly recommended（強烈建議）。strong 是形容詞；strength 是名詞；strengthen 是動詞。")]),
 ("報導：麵包店獲獎",
  "MAPLETON (April 2) — Golden Crust Bakery has won this year's Best Small Business award from the Mapleton Chamber of Commerce. The bakery, which opened just three years ago, was ___[1]___ for its use of local ingredients and its support of community events. ___[2]___\n\nOwner Lena Fischer said she was surprised by the news. \"We are a small team, and every one of us works hard,\" she said. \"This award really belongs to my staff.\"\n\nMs. Fischer plans to use the prize money to ___[3]___ a second oven, which will allow the bakery to increase production. The award ceremony will be held on April 20 at the Mapleton Hotel, and tickets are available to the ___[4]___.",
  [(["recognized", "recognizing", "recognition", "recognize"], "麵包店是「被表揚」的，was + 過去分詞的被動：was recognized for…。recognizing 是主動；recognition 是名詞；recognize 是原形。"),
   (["Every Saturday, it donates unsold bread to a local shelter.", "The Chamber of Commerce was established in 1952.", "Bread prices have risen across the region this year.", "Ms. Fischer previously worked as an accountant."],
    "句子插入題：前一句說獲獎原因之一是支持社區活動，接著舉例「每週六把沒賣完的麵包捐給收容所」最連貫。商會成立年份、麵包漲價都離題；Fischer 女士在下一段才第一次出現，這裡先用 Ms. Fischer 稱呼不合理。"),
   (["purchase", "purchasing", "purchased", "purchaser"], "to 後面接原形動詞：to purchase a second oven（購買第二台烤箱）。purchasing、purchased 不能接在不定詞 to 後面；purchaser 是名詞（買方）。"),
   (["public", "publicly", "publicity", "publish"], "the public（一般大眾）是固定說法：門票開放大眾購買。publicly 是副詞；publicity 是名詞（宣傳），和 available to 不搭；publish 是動詞。")]),
 ("備忘錄：新的報帳系統",
  "MEMO\nTo: All employees\nFrom: Finance Department\nDate: May 12\n\nStarting June 1, all travel expenses must be submitted through ExpenseNow, our new online system. The system will replace the paper forms that we ___[1]___ for the past ten years.\n\nWith ExpenseNow, you can photograph receipts with your phone and submit claims in minutes. ___[2]___, reimbursements will be processed within five business days instead of three weeks.\n\nTraining sessions will be held next week in Room 4B. ___[3]___ Employees who cannot attend may watch a recorded version on the company intranet. Paper forms will no longer be accepted ___[4]___ May 31.",
  [(["have used", "use", "will use", "are using"], "for the past ten years（過去十年來）搭配現在完成式：have used。use 是現在簡單式；will use 是未來式；are using 是現在進行式，都不能和 for the past ten years 搭配。"),
   (["In addition", "However", "Otherwise", "For example"], "前一句說新系統的好處（用手機拍收據、幾分鐘就能申請），這句再加一個好處（五個工作天內撥款），用 In addition（此外）。However 表示轉折；Otherwise（否則）、For example（例如）都不合。"),
   (["Each session will last about forty-five minutes.", "Receipts must be kept for seven years.", "Room 4B is currently being renovated.", "Our travel policy has not changed since 2015."],
    "句子插入題：前一句說下週在 4B 室舉辦訓練課程，接著說明每場課程的長度最連貫。4B 室正在整修，和在那裡上課矛盾；收據保存年限和差旅政策都離題。"),
   (["after", "until", "since", "during"], "「5 月 31 日之後」不再接受紙本表格：no longer… after May 31。until 搭配 no longer 會變成「到 5 月 31 日為止不再接受」，語意不合；since 要搭配完成式；during 後面接一段期間。")]),
]
